  "implementation_contract": [
    "Native Call/Invoke plans classify actual variadic operands after validating the fixed signature prefix and independent tail attributes.",
    "Only canonical direct llvm.va_start.p0, llvm.va_copy.p0 and llvm.va_end.p0 intrinsics receive owned cursor lowering; default promotions remain the frontend responsibility.",
    "The pinned LLVM22 unsized AS0-pointer dead_on_return promise is retained as a conservative nonexploited refinement. It grants no byval support.",
    "Raw GP/vector incoming banks are saved before use; RV64 variadic frame and CFI use the same80-byte header.",
    "Native .oc initial type checking remains before typed MIR lowering; native code generation remains owned, while LLVM still serves foreign parsing and verification."
  ],
